          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Win tricks to score points. First team to reach 31 or more wins. Four sevens in hand wins the game instantly. La Politaine (10-9-A of a suit) used to win three consecutive tricks scores an 11-point bonus.',
          gameplay: "1. **Lead**: Player to dealer's left leads. Winner of each trick leads the next. 2. **Play**: Any card may be led. Must follow suit if possible; if void, may play any card. No trumpsâ€”highest card of the suit led wins. 3. **La Politaine**: If a player holds 10-9-A of a suit and wins three consecutive tricks with them, announce before playing the first card; team scores 11-point bonus. 4. **Scoring**: At end of hand, count points: Aces 1 each; 10,9,K,Q,J 1/3 each; 8,7 nothing; last trick 1. Fractional points ignored; total 11 per hand. 5. **Winning**: First team to 31+ wins. Tie at 33: play another deal.",
          keyRules: [
            'No trumps. Highest card of the suit led wins the trick.',
            'Must follow suit when possible.',
            'Four sevens in one hand = immediate game win for that team.',
            'La Politaine: 10-9-A of a suit; must announce before first play; must win three consecutive tricks with those cards to score 11-point bonus.',
            'Card values: A=1; 10,9,K,Q,J=1/3 each; 8,7=0. Last trick=1.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Lead from your long suits to pull cards. Save high cards to win point-bearing tricks. If you have La Politaine, try to obtain the lead and win three tricks in a row with 10-9-A.',
          intermediate: 'Count points in tricks to know when you have enough. Signal partner (e.g. tap table = good in that suit) if playing with conventions. Discard low cards on opponent point tricks.',
          advanced: 'La Politaine is riskyâ€”you may not get the lead or may be forced to break the sequence. Some variants require leading the Ace first when playing La Politaine to guarantee at least one point in the first trick. Coordinate with partner to establish leads.',
          tips: [
            'If holding La Politaine, announce before playing the first card.',
            'Leading the Ace first from a Politaine guarantees the first trick is worth at least 1 point.',
            'Watch for four 7sâ€”they win the game before play begins.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
